            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue.\r\n\r\nCouple of clarifications:\r\n- On current commit (c4b6e6e) this seems to only happen if `require('mini.indentscope').setup()` is called after startup (like if lazy-loaded). So `nvim -u init-minimal.lua`:\r\n\r\n    - Works fine (has intro splash screen) with the following 'init-minimal.lua':\r\n\r\n        ```lua\r\n        -- Register 'mini.nvim' when it is in 'pack/*/opt'\r\n        vim.cmd.packadd('mini.nvim')\r\n        require('mini.indentscope').setup()\r\n        ``` \r\n\r\n    - Removes intro screen with the following 'init-minimal.lua':\r\n    \r\n        ```lua\r\n        vim.schedule(function()\r\n          vim.cmd.packadd('mini')\r\n          require('mini.indentscope').setup()\r\n        end)\r\n        ```\r\n- Same behavior is present before 1695f39 (specifically, on its parent 124b182): screen is removed with `schedule()`, present otherwise.\r\n- If indeed [lines for highlight group creation](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c4b6e6ede40578d5b94b557d62b6caf15d268dbf/lua/mini/indentscope.lua#L146-L150) are removed, intro screen is intact even with `schedule()`.\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell, the core problem here is that creating highlight group (either with `:hi` or with `vim.api.nvim_set_hl()`) causes screen redraw. As said in [this 6 year old comment](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/5881#issuecomment-270635733), that intro message is not a part of screen, so on any redraw event it gets removed. So this is not a problem of 'mini.indentscope' per se, but any module which creates highlight groups (like 'mini.jump' has this problem, but 'mini.bracketed' does not).\r\n\r\nSo I am not sure what can be done here. Highlight groups *should* be created for plugin to operate properly. They can all be created during startup, but that would affect its time and contradict with lazy loading of any module.",
